# Create slides with interactive 3D

<p class="hero-lead">This tutorial shows how to put interactive 3D models, typically made with OpenGL, in
your presentations: a model that turns, a simulation you tune, a curve you drag, live in the slide
while you speak. It works with the slide tools that show a web page, and with your own C++ code.</p>

