## How it works

<div class="outputs">
<div class="output"><div class="output-name">1. A web page</div><p>Your OpenGL program, compiled to WebAssembly, runs in a browser. Or a model file shown by a viewer.</p></div>
<div class="output"><div class="output-name">2. A frame in the slide</div><p>The slide shows that page in an <code>&lt;iframe&gt;</code>: HTML slides do it natively.</p></div>
<div class="output"><div class="output-name">3. Driven from the slide</div><p>Settings in its address, a panel, buttons in the slide, values sent back, the arrow keys kept.</p></div>
</div>

